---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = 'Life Story Wealth Planning · Alex Hilbert, Registered Investment Advisor, Scottsdale, Arizona';
const description = 'A small Scottsdale investment advisory firm run by Alex Hilbert, a Registered Investment Advisor and fiduciary. Active portfolio management for people who have already built their wealth.';

const personSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Person',
  name: 'Alex Hilbert',
  jobTitle: 'Registered Investment Advisor',
  worksFor: {
    '@type': 'FinancialService',
    name: 'Life Story Wealth Planning',
    url: 'https://lifestorywp.com',
  },
  address: {
    '@type': 'PostalAddress',
    addressLocality: 'Scottsdale',
    addressRegion: 'AZ',
    addressCountry: 'US',
  },
};

const firmSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FinancialService',
  name: 'Life Story Wealth Planning',
  url: 'https://lifestorywp.com',
  founder: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Alex Hilbert' },
  areaServed: { '@type': 'State', name: 'Arizona' },
  address: {
    '@type': 'PostalAddress',
    addressLocality: 'Scottsdale',
    addressRegion: 'AZ',
    addressCountry: 'US',
  },
};
---
<Base title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/">
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(personSchema)} />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(firmSchema)} />
  </Fragment>

  {/* No rail, this is a letter, not a table of contents */}

  <section class="titlepage">
    <div class="titlepage-grain" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="titlepage-glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="titlepage-corner titlepage-corner-tl" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="titlepage-corner titlepage-corner-tr" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="titlepage-corner titlepage-corner-bl" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="titlepage-corner titlepage-corner-br" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <div class="titlepage-monogram" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="mono-letters">AH</span>
      <span class="mono-line"></span>
      <span class="mono-label">Life Story · Est. 2024</span>
    </div>

    <div class="titlepage-inner">
      <p class="titlepage-eyebrow">        <span>A note from Alex Hilbert</span>      </p>

      <h1 class="titlepage-h1">
        <span class="line1 reveal-line" style="--d: 0.1s">What is this</span>
        <span class="line2 reveal-line" style="--d: 0.28s">money <em>for?</em></span>
      </h1>

      <p class="titlepage-lede reveal-line" style="--d: 0.5s">The question that comes before any portfolio decision. A short read for anyone who was handed my name by someone they trust.</p>

      <div class="titlepage-cta-row reveal-line" style="--d: 0.68s">
        <a class="cta" href="#letter">Start reading</a>
        <a class="cta-ghost" href="/about">Read about Alex</a>
      </div>

      <div class="titlepage-meta reveal-line" style="--d: 0.82s">
        <span>Written in Scottsdale, Arizona</span>
        <span class="meta-sep">·</span>
        <span>Fiduciary since 2012</span>
        <span class="meta-sep">·</span>
        <span>Last reviewed Sep 2026</span>
      </div>
    </div>

  </section>

  <div class="credbar">
    <div class="credbar-inner">
      <button type="button" class="cred-btn" data-target="ria">Registered Investment Advisor</button>
      <button type="button" class="cred-btn" data-target="fid">Fiduciary Standard</button>
      <button type="button" class="cred-btn" data-target="cust">Third-Party Custodian</button>
      <button type="button" class="cred-btn" data-target="fee">Fee-Aligned</button>
    </div>
    <div class="cred-expand" data-cred="ria" hidden>
      <p>
        <strong>Registered Investment Advisor.</strong> A specific US regulatory designation, not a job
        title anyone can adopt. It requires SEC or state registration and comes with legal obligations
        that don't apply to unregistered advisors, including the fiduciary standard described below.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="cred-expand" data-cred="fid" hidden>
      <p>
        <strong>Fiduciary Standard.</strong> A legal requirement to act in your interest ahead of my
        own. Most broker-dealers operate under the lower "suitability" standard, they only have to
        recommend products that are broadly suitable for your situation, not necessarily what's best
        for you. As a fiduciary I don't have that latitude.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="cred-expand" data-cred="cust" hidden>
      <p>
        <strong>Third-Party Custodian.</strong> Your assets are held at an independent custodian, not
        by my firm. I direct how the money in your account is invested. I cannot remove funds from it,
        to me or to anyone else. That structural separation is described in full on the Custody page.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="cred-expand" data-cred="fee" hidden>
      <p>
        <strong>Fee-Aligned.</strong> There is no management fee. I am paid only when your portfolio
        exceeds a defined threshold in a given quarter. If it doesn't, I don't get paid for that
        quarter. My incentives are aligned with yours by construction, not by promise.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <article class="letter" id="letter">
    <div class="letter-grain" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <div class="letter-column">
      <aside class="marginalia marginalia-recto">
        <span class="marginalia-label">Written for</span>
        <span class="marginalia-body">the reader who was handed my name by someone they trust.</span>
      </aside>

      <p class="letter-open">
        <span class="dropcap">M</span>ost portfolios sit still. Markets do not. When markets fall,
        the standard answer clients hear from their adviser is to do nothing.
      </p>

      <p class="letter-p">
        I do not think that is management. It is the absence of it. I built this firm to work the
        other way, to actually manage portfolios, reviewed and reconstituted every quarter, moved
        between asset classes as conditions change.
      </p>

      <aside class="marginalia marginalia-verso zermagen-mark-wrap">
        <svg class="zermagen-mark" viewBox="0 0 80 100" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
          <!-- Fortress crenellations across the top -->
          <path class="zm-crenel" d="M 10 4 L 10 14 L 20 14 L 20 4 L 30 4 L 30 14 L 40 14 L 40 4 L 50 4 L 50 14 L 60 14 L 60 4 L 70 4 L 70 14" />
          <!-- Shield body, outline curving to point at bottom -->
          <path class="zm-shield" d="M 10 14 L 70 14 L 70 46 C 70 68 58 82 40 92 C 22 82 10 68 10 46 Z" />
          <!-- Small central dot, the "guarded interior" -->
          <circle class="zm-core" cx="40" cy="48" r="2.5" />
        </svg>
        <span class="marginalia-label">Tzur Magen</span>
        <span class="marginalia-body">Hebrew for <em>fortress and shield</em>.</span>
      </aside>

      <p class="letter-p">
        The process has a name. I call it <strong>Tzur Magen</strong>. It is built around a single
        idea: <em>risk comes first.</em> Before I decide what to buy, I decide what could go wrong
        and how to guard against it.
      </p>

      <aside class="marginalia marginalia-recto risk-first-mark-wrap">
        <div class="risk-first-mark" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="rf-step rf-step-1">
            <span class="rf-num">01</span>
            <span class="rf-label">Risk</span>
          </div>
          <div class="rf-arrow"><span class="rf-arrow-head"></span></div>
          <div class="rf-step rf-step-2">
            <span class="rf-num">02</span>
            <span class="rf-label">Buy</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <span class="marginalia-label">Order matters</span>
        <span class="marginalia-body">Most advisers work the other way, buy first, worry about downside later.</span>
      </aside>

      <p class="letter-p">
        Putting risk first does not mean playing it safe. The standard way to reduce risk is to
        park half a portfolio in bonds and call it prudence, a parking brake left on. That is
        drag, not defense. My version is closer to steering: <em>dodging</em> the pothole rather
        than driving slowly enough to survive it. Avoid enough of the downside, capture most of
        the upside, and the long run takes care of itself, with less volatility, not more.
      </p>

      <figure class="pullquote-fig">
        <blockquote class="pullquote">
          <p>Markets are people first, and mathematics a distant third.</p>
        </blockquote>
        <figcaption class="pullquote-source">A. Hilbert</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <aside class="marginalia marginalia-recto">
        <span class="marginalia-label">See also</span>
        <span class="marginalia-body"><a href="/about">About</a>, the origin story: why I left Vanguard.</span>
      </aside>

      <p class="letter-p">
        Most of my clients came to me because someone they trust suggested it. If that is how you
        arrived here, this letter is written for you.
      </p>

      <p class="letter-p">
        I work with a small number of individuals, usually approaching retirement or already in
        it, usually more focused on keeping what they have built without forfeiting opportunities
        for growth.
      </p>

      <div class="two-columns">
        <div class="two-columns-col is-fit">
          <p class="two-columns-h">
            <span class="tc-mark" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M2 7 L6 11 L12 3" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            </span>
            Probably a fit if
          </p>
          <ul class="two-columns-list">
            <li>You've built your wealth. You want to keep what you've built and make sure it keeps serving you.</li>
            <li>You want a portfolio that responds to markets, not one left to their whims.</li>
            <li>You want to work directly with the person managing your money.</li>
            <li>You read carefully. You ask real questions. You take your time.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="two-columns-col is-miss">
          <p class="two-columns-h">
            <span class="tc-mark" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><line x1="3" y1="7" x2="11" y2="7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
            </span>
            Probably not, if
          </p>
          <ul class="two-columns-list">
            <li>You want a passive index portfolio, matched to a benchmark and left alone.</li>
            <li>You want to direct the trades in your account yourself.</li>
            <li>You want product recommendations paid for by commission.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="letter-note">
        If any of the right column describes you, there are firms that fit that better than I do,
        and I'll say so directly. <a href="/who-i-work-with">A fuller portrait is here →</a>
      </p>

      <div class="mid-cta">
        <p class="mid-cta-text">If the left column is you, the easiest way to start is a short call. First conversation is a conversation, no fee, no pressure.</p>
        <a class="cta cta-inline" href="/contact">Book a call with Alex</a>
      </div>

      <div class="differs">
        <p class="letter-question">So, what's actually different here?</p>
        <div class="differs-grid">
          <div class="differs-row">
            <div class="differs-them">
              <span class="differs-label">Standard adviser</span>
              <p>Charges a management fee whether the portfolio grows or shrinks.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="differs-me">
              <span class="differs-label">This firm</span>
              <p>No management fee. Paid only on gains above a defined threshold.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="differs-row">
            <div class="differs-them">
              <span class="differs-label">Standard adviser</span>
              <p>Sits on their hands when markets fall, "stay the course."</p>
            </div>
            <div class="differs-me">
              <span class="differs-label">This firm</span>
              <p>Reviews and reconstitutes the portfolio every quarter, moving as conditions change.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="differs-row">
            <div class="differs-them">
              <span class="differs-label">Standard adviser</span>
              <p>Earns commissions on recommended products.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="differs-me">
              <span class="differs-label">This firm</span>
              <p>No commissions on anything. Ever.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="differs-row">
            <div class="differs-them">
              <span class="differs-label">Standard adviser</span>
              <p>Answers to a corporate office. Managed by a team.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="differs-me">
              <span class="differs-label">This firm</span>
              <p>Answers to clients. Managed by me, directly.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="differs-note">These are structural facts, not marketing claims. Each is described in more detail on its own page.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="counts-on">
        <p class="letter-question">What can I actually promise you?</p>
        <ol class="counts-on-list">
          <li>
            <span class="counts-on-num">01</span>
            <span class="counts-on-body">
              You will always know where your money is. It sits in your own name, at a third-party
              custodian, and I cannot remove it.
            </span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="counts-on-num">02</span>
            <span class="counts-on-body">
              Every decision on your portfolio is mine. There is no committee to blame, no model to hide behind, no team to escalate to. When something works, I did it. When it does not, that is on me.
            </span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="counts-on-num">03</span>
            <span class="counts-on-body">
              You will hear from me quarterly, and any time positioning changes materially.
            </span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="counts-on-num">04</span>
            <span class="counts-on-body">
              I will say so directly if I am not the right fit for you, and I will point you at a
              firm that is.
            </span>
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p class="counts-on-note">Not returns. Not guarantees. Just what you can count on from me, as behaviour.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="fee-moment">
        <p class="letter-question">So, what does this cost?</p>

        <p class="fee-hook">
          There is no management fee. My incentives line up with yours by construction.
          I'm only paid based on how your portfolio grows.
        </p>

        <div class="fee-cards">
          <article class="fee-card fee-card-lose">
            <p class="fee-card-when">
              <span class="fee-card-mark" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><line x1="3.5" y1="7" x2="10.5" y2="7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
              </span>
              In a losing quarter
            </p>
            <p class="fee-card-answer">Potentially nothing.</p>
            <p class="fee-card-body">
              When the strategy does not exceed the defined threshold, I am not paid for that quarter.
              At all.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article class="fee-card fee-card-win">
            <p class="fee-card-when">
              <span class="fee-card-mark" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M7 3 L7 11 M3.5 7 L7 11 L10.5 7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
              </span>
              In a winning quarter
            </p>
            <p class="fee-card-answer">A share of the excess gain.</p>
            <p class="fee-card-body">
              When the strategy exceeds the threshold, I'm paid a share of the gain above it.
              Not commissions. Not fixed fees. A share.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <p class="fee-page-link">
          The exact wording, and what it means in plain language, is on the
          <a href="/fees">Fees page <span class="fee-page-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <figure class="custody-breakout">
      <div class="custody-corner tl" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="custody-corner tr" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="custody-corner bl" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="custody-corner br" aria-hidden="true"></div>

      <p class="custody-eyebrow">        <span>The safeguard</span>      </p>
      <p class="custody-question">And where is your money, exactly?</p>
      <h2 class="custody-statement">I never hold client money.</h2>

      <div class="custody-diagram-wrap" role="figure" aria-label="The three-party structural safeguard: you own the account, I direct how it's invested, an independent third-party custodian holds the assets. I cannot move funds.">
        <svg class="custody-diagram" viewBox="0 0 1000 520" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet">
          <!-- YOU box -->
          <g class="cd-node cd-you">
            <rect x="30" y="20" width="300" height="170" rx="3" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" />
            <text x="180" y="66" text-anchor="middle" class="cd-title">You</text>
            <line x1="105" y1="82" x2="255" y2="82" class="cd-underline" />
            <text x="180" y="118" text-anchor="middle" class="cd-body">The account is in</text>
            <text x="180" y="141" text-anchor="middle" class="cd-body">your own name.</text>
            <text x="180" y="169" text-anchor="middle" class="cd-body cd-body-quiet">Not the firm's. Not pooled.</text>
          </g>

          <!-- ME (Alex) box -->
          <g class="cd-node cd-me">
            <rect x="670" y="20" width="300" height="170" rx="3" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" />
            <text x="820" y="66" text-anchor="middle" class="cd-title">Me</text>
            <line x1="745" y1="82" x2="895" y2="82" class="cd-underline" />
            <text x="820" y="118" text-anchor="middle" class="cd-body">I direct how it's</text>
            <text x="820" y="141" text-anchor="middle" class="cd-body">invested.</text>
            <text x="820" y="169" text-anchor="middle" class="cd-body cd-body-quiet">I cannot remove funds.</text>
          </g>

          <!-- Arrow from YOU down-right to CUSTODIAN -->
          <g class="cd-arrow">
            <path d="M 180 205 L 180 275 L 400 275 L 400 348" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" />
            <polygon points="400,352 394,340 406,340" />
            <text x="235" y="266" class="cd-arrow-label">Owns</text>
          </g>

          <!-- Arrow from ME down-left to CUSTODIAN -->
          <g class="cd-arrow">
            <path d="M 820 205 L 820 275 L 600 275 L 600 348" fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" />
            <polygon points="600,352 594,340 606,340" />
            <text x="710" y="266" class="cd-arrow-label">Directs</text>
          </g>

          <!-- Central label: the crux -->
          <text x="500" y="316" text-anchor="middle" class="cd-crux">Your assets live here, not with me.</text>

          <!-- CUSTODIAN box (larger, emphasised) -->
          <g class="cd-node cd-cust">
            <rect x="130" y="350" width="740" height="150" rx="3" fill="none" stroke-width="2" />
            <text x="500" y="398" text-anchor="middle" class="cd-title cd-title-cust">Third-party custodian</text>
            <line x1="390" y1="415" x2="610" y2="415" class="cd-underline cd-underline-cust" />
            <text x="500" y="445" text-anchor="middle" class="cd-body">An independent institution.</text>
            <text x="500" y="470" text-anchor="middle" class="cd-body cd-body-italic">My firm never holds your assets.</text>
          </g>
        </svg>
      </div>

      <p class="custody-footer">
        That distinction is the single most important structural safeguard in how I've built
        this firm. <a href="/custody">The full explanation is here →</a>
      </p>
    </figure>

    <div class="letter-column">
      <div class="how-starts">
        <p class="letter-question">And how does this actually start?</p>
        <ol class="how-starts-steps">
          <li>
            <span class="how-step-num">One</span>
            <div class="how-step-body">
              <h4 class="how-step-h">Read the <a href="/about">About page</a>.</h4>
              <p>The Vanguard-to-independent origin story, what "fiduciary" means in practice, and how to verify me before we speak.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="how-step-num">Two</span>
            <div class="how-step-body">
              <h4 class="how-step-h">Check whether we're a fit.</h4>
              <p>I work with a small number of qualified clients, accounts held at a defined minimum and a limited amount of availability at any given time. Straightforward to self-check before we spend a call on it.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="how-step-num">Three</span>
            <div class="how-step-body">
              <h4 class="how-step-h">Book a call.</h4>
              <p>No fee, no pressure, no obligation. A first conversation is a conversation. Nothing else.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>
        <div class="how-starts-cta-row">
          <a class="cta" href="/contact">Book a call</a>
          <a class="cta-ghost cta-ghost-ink" href="/about">Read about Alex first</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="signoff">
        <p class="signoff-line">Alex Hilbert</p>
        <p class="signoff-meta">Scottsdale, Arizona · Fiduciary since 2012</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
